From bce26eae74cf33f6e4b435bf2162ea51fe8f24d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chandan <chandan@medpath.dev>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 18:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sample Collection: redesign for high-frequency operational
 use (UX review)

Addresses the UX review point-by-point:

- Patient identity dominates: 20px/700 name, accent patient ID, large
  status chip (Awaiting Collection / Collected), avatar status ring.
  Related fields (mobile, doctor, fasting, priority) grouped below a
  divider instead of one flat text block.
- Priority gets real colour language: routine = blue, urgent = amber,
  stat = red, matching the existing status-pill palette.
- Sample tubes are now cards: full-height colour strip, 'Required'
  chip, larger barcode (+35%), and per-tube Print/Preview/Reprint
  icon actions.
- Collection panel reordered as a workflow (Collector -> Time ->
  Sample type -> Notes -> Print Labels -> Mark as Collected), with
  Mark as Collected promoted to a 52px primary CTA with shadow/hover
  lift, and Print Labels kept as the secondary/outline action.
- Workflow trail replaced with a full lifecycle timeline (Registered
  through Report Ready) using a dot-and-connecting-line pattern with
  done/active/pending states, instead of 4 nav-like step chips.
- Empty space below now holds a Collection Checklist (identity
  verified, barcode attached, tube mixed, sealed, consent) with a
  live completed-count.
- Empty state copy/icon updated to 'No Samples Pending'.
- Accessibility/interaction passes: readonly inputs get more
  contrast, focus-visible rings on inputs/checklist items, 40px+
  icon touch targets, hover/press feedback on buttons and tube
  cards, and keyboard shortcuts (Enter = Mark as Collected, Ctrl/Cmd+P
  = Print Labels).

Out of scope for this patch (affects other screens, not just Sample
Collection): sidebar section grouping, global search bar shortcuts,
and top-header operational widgets (scanner/printer/queue status).
Happy to take those on separately if wanted.
